---

<Article
  title="Wingspan Pocket vs Wingspan: Every Difference Explained"
  description="No birdfeeder, no habitats, no rounds — how the 2026 pocket edition actually plays compared to the original Wingspan."
  game="wingspan-pocket"
  gameTitle="Wingspan Pocket"
  category="Rules"
  product="wingspan-pocket-insert"
  publishDate="2026-07-28"
>
  <p>
    Wingspan Pocket, released by Stonemaier Games in July 2026, is not a travel
    repack of Wingspan — it's a genuinely different game designed by Elizabeth
    Hargrave, the original Wingspan designer. If you know the big game, almost
    every system has been rebuilt for the small box. Here's exactly what changed.
  </p>

  <KeyTakeaway answer="Wingspan Pocket removes the birdfeeder dice, habitat mats, and round structure entirely. You activate a single row of cards, food lives on the back of bird cards, and the game ends when someone plays their sixth bird — all in 25–35 minutes. It's a standalone game, not an expansion." />

  <h2>The Big Differences</h2>

  <ComparisonTable title="Wingspan vs Wingspan Pocket">
    <table class="w-full text-sm">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">Feature</th>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">Wingspan</th>
          <th class="text-left p-3 bg-bark/[0.02] font-heading font-semibold text-bark/70">Wingspan Pocket</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5">
          <td class="p-3 font-semibold">Play time</td><td class="p-3">40–70 minutes</td><td class="p-3">25–35 minutes</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5">
          <td class="p-3 font-semibold">Food source</td><td class="p-3">Birdfeeder dice tower</td><td class="p-3">Back side of bird cards</td>
        </tr>
        <tr class="border-t border-bark/5">
          <td class="p-3 font-semibold">Habitats</td><td class="p-3">3 rows (forest, grassland, wetland)</td><td class="p-3">One single row of cards</td>
